### 2026-08-19 — Bug fix: Waafi error message swallowed + invitation shown after payment failure

Root cause 1 (error message swallowed):

`getApiErrorMessage` had a subtle priority inversion: it called `firstValidationMessage(data.errors)` before checking `data.message`. For payment charge failures, Laravel returns `{ success: false, message: "Insufficient balance", errors: {} }`. `firstValidationMessage` found nothing in the empty `errors` object and returned null — then `data.message` was checked. In this case the message WOULD have been returned. However the actual loss occurred in `ParticipantWaafiPayment.handleCharge`: on a HTTP 200 with `payment.status = "failed"`, the code used `payment.failure_reason || payment.failure_code || "Payment failed."`. If `failure_reason` is null and `failure_code` is null, the fallback "Payment failed." was returned — hiding the real provider message. Additionally, the `onFailure` callback in `RegistrationDetail` only called `toast.error(reason)` — the message appeared for a few seconds and then vanished. No persistent error state was kept on the page.

Root cause 2 (invitation visible after failure):

The invitation canvas was gated on `!isPaymentPending`. `payment_status === "failed"` and `"refunded"` are not `"pending"`, so `isPaymentPending === false` — the invitation and QR code were rendered as if the ticket were valid.

Files:

- `src/lib/apiError.ts` — fixed `getApiErrorMessage` priority: now checks `data.message` BEFORE `data.errors.*` (domain failures from Laravel/Waafi live in `data.message`). Added dedicated `getChargeFailureMessage(payment)` helper that extracts the best human text from `payment.failure_reason` then `payment.failure_code` (with readable capitalisation), falling back to "Payment was not completed." Never returns empty string.
- `src/components/participant/ParticipantWaafiPayment.tsx` — now has three internal states: `idle` (phone form), `charging` (spinner), `failed` (inline error block). On any failure path (HTTP 200 failed, 400, timeout, network), the error message is rendered visibly inside the panel with a "Try again" button and optional "Check status" button. `onFailure` is now optional — component handles display itself. Added `onCheckStatus` prop. Imports `getChargeFailureMessage` for the 200-failed path.
- `src/pages/RegistrationDetail.tsx` — replaced `canDownload()` with `hasValidTicket(status, paymentStatus)` which returns true only for `payment_status = "paid"` or `"not_required"` AND `status` not `waitlisted`/`cancelled`. Added `isPaymentFailed` and `isPaymentRefunded` derived booleans. `ParticipantWaafiPayment` now shown for both `pending` and `failed` states (retry uses same participation ID). Added `refunded` explanation block. Invitation canvas, QR, and Download PDF only render when `ticketValid === true`. "Check status" button visible for both `pending` and `failed` payment states. `onCheckStatus={load}` passed to payment component so its "Check status" button also re-fetches.

New ticket eligibility rule:

```typescript
function hasValidTicket(status, paymentStatus): boolean {
  if (status === "cancelled" || status === "waitlisted") return false;
  return paymentStatus === "paid" || paymentStatus === "not_required";
}
```

statusMeta now handles all payment_status values:
  - pending → "Awaiting payment" (orange)
  - failed  → "Payment failed" (red)
  - refunded → "Payment refunded" (muted)
  - paid / status=paid → "Confirmed · Paid" (green)

Verification:

- `npx tsc --noEmit` — pass
- `npm run build` — pass

### 2026-08-19 — State machine fix: correct paid-registration flow + stranded pending payment resume

Root cause (first regression): `AuroraBackdrop` is background-only (no `children` prop). All three non-form steps (`WaafiPhoneStep`, `SuccessCard`, `PaymentFailCard`) were wrapped as children of `<AuroraBackdrop>` and silently swallowed.

Root cause (second regression, this pass): `handlePaymentCancel` reset step to `{ kind: "form" }`. Since the participation already exists at that point, a re-submit would get a "already has an active participation" 400 and strand the user. Cancel now navigates to `/registrations/{id}` so the user can resume payment from the detail page.

Root cause (third regression, this pass): `/registrations/:id` showed the invitation canvas even while `payment_status === pending`, presenting the ticket as valid before payment was confirmed.

Files:

- `src/components/participant/ParticipantWaafiPayment.tsx` (new) — shared EVC Plus / WaafiPay UI component. Receives `participationId`, `eventName`, `ticketName`, `amount`, `currency`, `brandColor`, `isDark`, `onSuccess`, `onFailure`, `onCancel`. Handles the 210s charge call, elapsed timer, "already paid" race recovery, "already pending" message, network-timeout uncertainty message. Does NOT create participations or hold backend business rules.
- `src/pages/Register.tsx` — removed local `WaafiPhoneStep` component; replaced with `ParticipantWaafiPayment`. `handlePaymentCancel` now navigates to `/registrations/{participation.id}` instead of resetting to `{ kind: "form" }`. Removed `Phone` icon import (no longer used in this file).
- `src/pages/RegistrationDetail.tsx` — removed `InlinePayPanel` component; replaced with `ParticipantWaafiPayment` (shared). Invitation canvas section (`Your invitation`, QR, Download PDF) is now gated behind `!isPaymentPending` — it is hidden entirely until payment is confirmed. `onFailure` callback surfaces the error via `toast.error`. Removed `chargeParticipation`, `getParticipation`, `AnimatePresence`, `Input`, `Label`, `Phone` imports (no longer needed in this file); added `toast` import.

Corrected registration state machine (Register.tsx):

1. User submits form → `POST /participant/participations`
2. `status === "waitlisted"` → `step = { kind: "success", waitlisted: true }` — waitlist card shown; no QR, no payment
3. `payment_status === "not_required" | "paid"` → `step = { kind: "success", waitlisted: false }` + `navigate("/registrations/{id}")` after 2.2s — explicit "You're registered!" confirmation
4. `payment_status === "pending"` → `step = { kind: "waafi", participation }` — `ParticipantWaafiPayment` shown immediately; form never goes blank
5. Waafi approved → `step = { kind: "success" }` + navigate to `/registrations/{id}` after 2.2s
6. Waafi failed → `step = { kind: "payment_failed", reason }` — retry button returns to step 4
7. User cancels Waafi → navigate to `/registrations/{participation.id}` (participation persists; user can resume from detail page)

Pending-payment resume (RegistrationDetail.tsx):

- When `payment_status === pending` and not waitlisted/cancelled, `ParticipantWaafiPayment` is shown prominently.
- `onSuccess` calls `load()` which re-fetches `/participant/participations/{id}/invitation`; page refreshes to confirmed state and reveals invitation canvas + QR.
- "Check status" button (already present in the status card) calls `load()` — if backend now reports paid, page immediately shows invitation.
- QR code, invitation canvas, Download PDF, and "Your invitation" heading are all hidden until `payment_status !== "pending"`.

Verification:

- `npx tsc --noEmit` — pass
- `npm run build` — pass

